lzug-admin backup restore - Restore a protected backup.

Restore a complete protected backup after validation. Replacing non-empty state also requires --replace.

Usage:
  lzug-admin [global options] backup restore --artifact NAME [options]

Command options:
  --artifact NAME          Protected artifact name inside the application data area. Required.
  --replace                Confirm replacement of a non-empty installation. Default: false. Danger-zone confirmation.

Secure input:
  stdin              Private recipient key read only from standard input.

Confirmation:
  Requires an interactive terminal confirmation or --force.
  --replace is a separate danger-zone confirmation and is never implied by --force.

Transport:
  Versioned request through the shared Docker/Podman container transport.

Output:
  Successful human output is silent; JSON includes the validated restore result.
  --verbose adds the secret-free progress and result summary on stderr.
  --json uses the declared projected result contract on stdout.

Examples:
  printf 'PRIVATE_KEY' | lzug-admin --container lzug backup restore --artifact backup.lzug --force
  printf 'PRIVATE_KEY' | lzug-admin --container lzug backup restore --artifact backup.lzug --replace --force
